+# RetroAchievements parity audit
+
+Parity with existing implementations is the minimum requirement. Source implementation,
+host tests, packaged builds and console acceptance are separate evidence levels.
+
+## Pinned references
+
+- xeRAbora OPL `ra`: `fa2d2e42` (Mode 6 snapshot tick), following PS1 commit
+  `531aad4584d65d1779b744739b81402150c7669c`.
+- Caduceus wrapper `main`: `cc1713a8`; its OPL snapshot is
+  `2a98a9d7361f8e33f421244bc88c318eab3bdf2f` (`opl-snapshot`).
+- RiptOPL baseline: `19028f357b5675a18a213dc6717cb5e23f163bf0`, Beta 3841.
+
+- ORBIT v1.0.2: `7a88a6a5fdc935001d977497460716762edef404`, archive SHA-256 `a5cf88e2f27d3745b01c93d6d691b162972749b35452a38461046a02b3f178a5`. Existing external RA runtime discovered after the initial narrow OPL audit.
+
+## Capability comparison
+
+| Capability | Reference | RiptOPL implementation | Remaining work |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| PS2 local images, support hashing/watch lists, snapshots | xeRAbora | Present for embedded-core BDM/MMCE; historical USB/MMCE hardware evidence | Current-client console regression coverage |
+| Physical PS2 disc support/launch | xeRAbora | Present, separate RA disc actions | Console acceptance |
+| USB PS1 POPStarter achievements | xeRAbora alpha.16 | Present, reader/module injection and image-identity guards | FAT32/exFAT console acceptance |
+| Mode 6 keeps achievements while disabling IGR | xeRAbora alpha.17 | Present, dedicated snapshot tick and reset guard | Current-build console acceptance |
+| Passive SMB telemetry and startup hold-off | Caduceus | Present; no RA socket/RX-ring consumption on SMB/HTTP, 30-second sender hold-off | Sustained network-game console acceptance; older upstream failures remain relevant |
+| Account/game achievement browser and pairing | Caduceus | Present, explicit companion host, session checks and browser | End-to-end console acceptance |
+| Gold unlock pulse | xeRAbora/Caduceus | Present | Current-build console regression coverage |
+| In-game title/points card | Caduceus release builds | Explicit default-Off Caduceus experimental opt-in | Console acceptance and safe GS transfer ownership remain open |
+| Raw UDP notice fits received frame | Caduceus snapshot | Restored; production regression and all six builds passed at `b4a1708f` | Current-build console regression coverage |
+| Neutrino/UDPFS PS2 telemetry | ORBIT v1.0.2, upstream console telemetry evidence | RA-only pinned runtime; Xerabora and Caduceus (same wire protocol to the engine); direct values <=1,216 bytes, chain tails ignored as in ORBIT; UDP storage reuses its stack | Fresh exact-head builds/packages, review and console acceptance; first-time UDP identification remains outstanding |
+| Non-USB PS1 telemetry | No integration found in these pinned references | Unavailable | Extension beyond the verified reference baseline |
+
+## Confirmed receiver correction
+
+`ra_drain_rx` bounded the declared UDP payload by its 256-byte scratch buffer but
+did not bound it by the actual descriptor length. A truncated frame could therefore
+pass stale bytes from a previous packet to the unlock/reset parser. The reference
+has `RA_HDR_LEN + up <= len`; restore it without changing socket/RX ownership.
+The production-function harness exercises stale tails, one-byte truncation,
+complete/padded packets, empty and oversized lengths, and terminator capacity.
+
+## Card parity is not an enable-flag change
+
+The reference card writes an IMAGE transfer into the game's displayed framebuffer.
+Checking a free GIF DMA channel and an idle GIF status does not establish ownership
+of the GS transfer registers across paths or an outstanding game IMAGE transfer.
+The reference documents physical-console display evidence, flicker, and a reported
+freeze followed by interrupt-safe/cache-work refinements. Those observations do not
+prove general transfer safety. The default remains the pulse. The explicit
+experimental opt-in makes the upstream-style renderer available with an in-UI
+risk notice; it does not establish safe ownership or console acceptance.
+
+The [Sony EE User's Manual v6.0](https://github.com/ninjadynamics/PS2Docs/blob/main/EE_Users_Manual.pdf),
+GIF_STAT reference (printed p. 164), distinguishes
+PATH3 interruption, pause, path masks and GS-to-EE direction from queued/active
+paths and FIFO occupancy. The experimental refusal mask now includes those
+states. The host rasterizer harness checks each mask bit independently and
+resumes submission after clearing the state. This closes specific refusal gaps;
+it does not solve ownership of GS transfer registers.
+
+## Event snapshot correction
+
+The production pulse previously consumed the DMA event's sequence and kind
+directly after checking its commit word. Copy the event first and validate both
+the copied commit and the live sequence/commit before changing notification or
+reset state. The experimental card now also validates the copied commit, which
+its existing live checks omitted. Deterministic host injection covers a new
+event arriving after the copy and a copy containing an uncommitted tail; neither
+may consume the sequence or trigger reset. A subsequent complete event remains
+processable. These checks establish the event contract, not GS timing safety.
+
+## Build isolation
+
+All telemetry, companion protocols, browser and RA-only strings must stay inside
+RETROACHIEVEMENTS builds. Shared POPS file hygiene is not a telemetry dependency.
+Do not copy a reference's unguarded RA core into ordinary builds.
+
+## Experimental runtime opt-in
+
+`ra_experimental_cards` defaults to 0, resets to Off on a missing config key,
+and accepts only integer 1 as enabled. Both interactive and autolaunch config
+readers use the same helper. The Network control is selectable only with
+Caduceus telemetry enabled. Only opted-in tracked Caduceus PS2 launches reserve
+the aligned packet; allocation-fence refusal routes events and VBLANK handling
+to the pulse. No new release flavour or EE-core config layout is introduced.
+The setting and its risk/help strings are RA-only.
+
+
+## Release acceptance and evidence
+
+The implementation build at `b4a1708f1c73461b964aac37c46477a93b8dc907`
+passed all six flavour builds, formatting and all applicable host jobs in
+[run 38194512093](https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/actions/runs/38194512093).
+Standard linked-binary checks reject all `gRA` globals; RA checks require the
+experimental-setting global. These checks do not establish console acceptance.
+
+The matching [RA artifact](https://github.com/NathanNeurotic/Open-PS2-Loader/actions/runs/38194512093/artifacts/11722644208)
+is a CI artifact, not a published release. Record the actual ELF/build identifier,
+console model, source device/filesystem, companion version and result for each
+console case below. Historical results do not count as this build's acceptance.
+
+| Console case | Required observation | Current evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Fresh RA configuration | Cards start Off; companion pairing and game identification succeed | Host config tests passed; console pending |
+| Embedded OPL PS2 launch from USB and MMCE | Watch list loads; snapshots reach companion; an achievement notice is delivered | Source/host/build checks passed; console pending |
+| Physical PS2 disc | Disc is identified and tracked through the RA disc launch action | Console pending |
+| SMB PS2 launch | Passive telemetry survives startup hold-off and sustained gameplay without disrupting game reads | Console pending |
+| USB POPStarter on FAT32 and exFAT | Correct VCD identity and watch data reach companion; achievement delivery succeeds | Console pending; PS1 console cards are outside this implementation |
+| Mode 6 | Tracking continues while controller IGR remains disabled | Host tests passed; console pending |
+| Normal IGR | Reset works after tracked gameplay and leaves the next launch usable | Host tests passed; console pending |
+| Experimental cards Off/On | Off uses pulse; On displays title/points; changing and saving persists across restart | Host routing/config tests passed; console pending; GS ownership remains unresolved |
+| Ordinary build | Launch/settings work without RA configuration or a running companion | Linked isolation checks passed; console pending |
+
+CodeRabbit completed the receiver/event/GIF fixes at `a1f586f1` with 0 issues.
+The full committed review including the runtime opt-in at `b4a1708f` has not
+completed: the latest retry returned `rate_limit`, a 16-minute wait, and no
+assigned organization seat for usage-based reviews. Retry after the service's
+wait period or resolve the seat/API-key prerequisite; do not reuse the earlier
+review as approval of the new setting.
+
+Before publishing:
+
+1. Complete the review of the final code and address confirmed issues.
+2. Record console acceptance, including any remaining experimental-card failures.
+   Keep cards default Off and retain the flicker/freeze warning.
+3. Verify the final PR head and its checks, then merge the coherent PR #916.
+4. Verify the release workflow's exact source commit, packaged RA and ordinary
+   assets, and publication state. A green build or downloadable CI artifact alone
+   is not release publication.
+5. Verify the generated live RetroAchievements page after docs-sync runs. Update
+   the wiki to match the shipped guide; no automatic wiki synchronization has
+   been established. Describe the ORBIT Neutrino handoff with its direct-watch,
+   saved-identity and static-IP limits; non-USB PS1 RA telemetry remains
+   unavailable, and PS1 notices remain companion-only.
